    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-65410",
      "knowledge_point_id": "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha ={sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha ={sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha -{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1} & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha -1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression by factoring it out, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha } & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha (\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha \\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha .\n$$",
